      "end": 949,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "AmINext\n#AmINext is a social media campaign that was launched on September 5 , 2014 by a Canadian Inuit woman named Holly Jarrett in order to call attention to the high rate of missing and murdered Indigenous women in Canada . Jarrett 's hashtag campaign was launched following the release of her Change.org petition in August of 2014 calling for a government inquiry into the high rate of missing and murdered Indigenous women . Social media users participate in the hashtag campaign by posting photographs of themselves holding up signs displaying the hashtag and by including a short message about why they are participating . The campaign was created in response to the deaths of Loretta Saunders , Jarrett 's cousin , and Tina Fontaine , a 15-year-old Aboriginal girl , among others . For over a decade , Indigenous activists have called for a government inquiry into the disproportionate rate of violence perpetuated against Indigenous women ."
